DocHelp_BaseControls = 
tc_orange+'BASIC GAME CONTROLS'+tc_default+tc_doccpt
tc_docbr
'The majority of your control during the game is through using your mouse. The mouse performs the following actions:'
tc_docbr+'- SELECTION: the "'+iAct_1_hk+'" is used to select units, buildings, command buttons and points of action (locations where orders are carried out).'
tc_docbr+'- AUTO COMMANDS: when you have a unit or group selected, the "'+iAct_2_hk+'" can be used to issue intelligent commands that will automatically be carried out.'
tc_docbr
tc_docbr
tc_orange+'CAMERA MOVEMENT'+tc_default+tc_doccpt
tc_docbr
'Possible ways to move the game camera include:'
tc_docbr+'- using keyboard arrow keys;'
tc_docbr+'- clicking and holding the "'+iAct_3_hk+'";'
tc_docbr+'- moving the cursor to the edges of the screen (this option can be enabled or disabled in the game settings).'
tc_docbr+'The speed of camera movement can be adjusted in the game settings.'
tc_docbr
tc_docbr
tc_orange+'BASE CONSTRUCTION'+tc_default+tc_doccpt
tc_docbr
'You must have at least one builder to build a base. Switch the control panel to "'+str_ui_Tab[tab_Buildings]+'" tab and click on the building icon to select the type of building you need(or press the associated hotkey).'
'If the requirements for the selected building type are not met, the game will display an error message; otherwise, the game will draw the building`s sprite and a circle around the mouse cursor.'
'The radius of the circle is the radius of the building. If the circle is red - the building needs more space, if it is blue - the build place is too far away from the nearest builder, if it is green - the building can be built here.'
'To deselect a building type, press "'+iAct_2_hk+'".'
str_ui_BuildHint
'To cancel the construction of a building, select it and issue the "'+str_dscr[iAct_Control_UProdCncl]+'" or "'+str_dscr[iAct_Control_UDestroy]+'" order.'
str_doc_NoteMaxBuilders+'.'
tc_docbr+'NOTE: losing your buildings affect your construction system into short cooldown effect.'
tc_docbr+str_ui_BuildTip
tc_docbr
tc_docbr
tc_orange+'UNIT PRODUCTION'+tc_default+tc_doccpt
tc_docbr
'Any unit may be built if the player has at least one building capable of producing that type of unit, and the unit`s other requirements are met.'
'Switch the control panel to "'+str_ui_Tab[tab_Units]+'" tab and click on the unit icon(or press the associated hotkey or hover your mouse over the unit icon and scroll the "'+iAct_4_hk+'").'
'If the requirements for the selected unit type are not met, the game will display an error message.'
'If no unit production building is selected - the game sends the production order to nearest unbusy production building, otherwise it sends the order to nearest unbusy selected production buildings.'
'It is impossible to create a unit production queue.'
'To cancel unit production process, click "'+iAct_2_hk+'" on the unit icon or select production buildings and issue then "'+str_dscr[iAct_Control_UProdCncl]+'" order.'
tc_docbr
tc_docbr
tc_orange+'UPGRADES PRODUCTION'+tc_default+tc_doccpt
tc_docbr
'Go to the "'+str_ui_Tab[tab_Upgrades]+'" tab in the Control Panel and click the upgrade icon. If the requirements for the selected upgrade type are not met, the game will display an error message.'
'If no upgrade production facility is selected - the game sends the production order to any nearest unbusy production facility, otherwise it sends the order to nearest unbusy selected production facilities.'
'It is impossible to create an upgrade production queue.'
'To cancel upgrade production process, click "'+iAct_2_hk+'" on the upgrade icon or select production buildings and issue then "'+str_dscr[iAct_Control_UProdCncl]+'" order.'
tc_docbr

